# Bug: `kanso test store` refuses the module that `kanso check store`
# accepts, and this test reads nothing from it.
#
# Run from bugs/test_refuses_what_check_accepts:
#   kanso check store    prints `store: ok`
#   kanso test store     error[exhaustive]: this can be a none and
#                        `store/ref_or_next` has no arm for it
#                        --> store/store.kso:27:40, with no source line
#
# should: the same verdict from both verbs. `at.value` is always a
#   `ref_value` record (both `followed` arms build one), so check's ok is
#   right and test's refusal is wrong. ugit's store/names.kso hit this at
#   `get_ref first .> (at -> ref_or_next at.value rest name)`; the port
#   carries a `ref_or_next none` arm that can never run, to get its tests
#   to compile.

test_nothing = 1 == 1
